          "what": "crankcase vent",
          "value": "Service at 12,000 Miles"
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        "Compression is psi at cranking speed with throttle wide open; cylinders may vary by at most 20 lbs.",
        "Timing is set at idle with the vacuum advance line disconnected and plugged. A = A.T.D.C., B = B.T.D.C.",
        "Mechanical valve lash is set with the engine at operating temperature and running.",
        "Set idle with automatic transmissions in drive. On air-conditioned cars set idle with the A/C off, except where marked *.",
        "V8 distributor: change the cam lubricator end for end every 12,000 miles and replace it at 24,000 miles.",
        "Fuel filter: replace the element in the carburetor inlet every 12 months or 12,000 miles, whichever comes first.",
        "Caution: the air cleaner also acts as a flame arrestor if the engine backfires; keep it installed unless removal is needed for repair or service.",
        "Paper air cleaner element: at the first 12,000 miles inspect for dust leaks, holes or damage and replace if needed; if good, rotate it 180° from its original position. Replace at 24,000 miles. Do not wash, oil, tap or blow it out with an air hose. Replace a \"Bowtie\" filter, if fitted, every 24,000 miles.",
        "Polyurethane element: every 12,000 miles clean in solvent such as kerosene, squeeze dry, soak in engine oil, squeeze out, then wring in a clean dry cloth to remove excess oil.",
        "Flame arrestor (in the base of the air cleaner): every 12,000 miles clean with kerosene or suitable solvent and dry with compressed air."
      ],
